{"id":"mahabharata-1-036","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":36,"title":"षट्त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 36 · Parikshit insults the silent sage Shamika","summary":{"en":"The bard explains Jaratkaru's name and austerity, then tells how King Parikshit, exhausted from a hunt, questioned the sage Shamika, who kept a vow of silence. Angered, the king draped a dead snake on his shoulder, and the youth Krisha taunted Shamika's son Shringin with it.","kn":"ಜರತ್ಕಾರುವಿನ ಹೆಸರು ಮತ್ತು ತಪಸ್ಸನ್ನು ವಿವರಿಸಿ, ಬೇಟೆಯಿಂದ ದಣಿದ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿತರಾಜನು ಮೌನವ್ರತದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದ ಶಮೀಕ ಋಷಿಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರಶ್ನಿಸಿದ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ರಾಜನು ಸತ್ತ ಹಾವನ್ನು ಅವರ ಹೆಗಲಿಗೆ ಹಾಕಿದನು; ಕೃಶನು ಅದರಿಂದ ಶಮೀಕನ ಮಗ ಶೃಂಗಿಯನ್ನು ಹಂಗಿಸಿದನು.","hi":"सूत जरत्कारु के नाम और तप का वर्णन कर बताते हैं कि शिकार से थके राजा परीक्षित ने मौनव्रती ऋषि शमीक से प्रश्न किया। उत्तर न मिलने पर क्रुद्ध राजा ने उनके कन्धे पर मरा साँप डाल दिया, और कृश ने इसी बात पर शमीक के पुत्र शृङ्गी को ताना मारा।","te":"జరత్కారుని పేరు, తపస్సు వివరించి, వేటతో అలసిన పరీక్షిన్మహారాజు మౌనవ్రతంలో ఉన్న శమీక ఋషిని ప్రశ్నించిన కథ చెబుతాడు. కోపించిన రాజు చచ్చిన పామును ఆయన భుజంపై వేశాడు; కృశుడు దానితో శమీకుని కుమారుడు శృంగిని ఎగతాళి చేశాడు.","ta":"ஜரத்காருவின் பெயரையும் தவத்தையும் விளக்கி, வேட்டையால் களைத்த பரீக்ஷித் மன்னன் மௌன விரதத்திலிருந்த ஶமீக முனிவரிடம் கேள்வி கேட்ட கதையைச் சொல்கிறார். கோபமுற்ற மன்னன் இறந்த பாம்பை அவர் தோளில் போட்டான்; க்ருஶன் அதைக் கொண்டு ஶமீகரின் மகன் ஶ்ருங்கியை ஏளனம் செய்தான்.","ml":"ജരത്കാരുവിന്റെ പേരും തപസ്സും ഗായകൻ വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു; പിന്നെ വേട്ടയാടി ക്ഷീണിച്ച പരീക്ഷിത്ത് രാജാവ്, മൗനവ്രതം പാലിച്ചിരുന്ന ശമീകൻ ഋഷിയോട് ചോദ്യം ചോദിക്കുന്നു. കോപിച്ച രാജാവ് ചത്ത പാമ്പിനെ ഋഷിയുടെ തോളിൽ ഇടുന്നു; കൃശൻ എന്ന യുവാവ് അത് കണ്ട് ശമീകന്റെ പുത്രനായ ശൃംഗിയെ പരിഹസിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.36; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"शौनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"जरत्कारुरिति प्रोक्तं यत्त्वया सूतनन्दन ।\nइच्छाम्येतदहं तस्य ऋषेः श्रोतुं महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You spoke of the name Jaratkaru, son of Suta. I wish to hear about that great sage."}},{"n":2,"text":"किं कारणं जरत्कारोर्नामैतत्प्रथितं भुवि ।\nजरत्कारुनिरुक्तं त्वं यथावद्वक्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why is this name Jaratkaru known on earth? Please explain the meaning of the name properly."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"जरेति क्षयमाहुर्वै दारुणं कारुसंज्ञितम् ।\nशरीरं कारु तस्यासीत्तत्स धीमाञ्शनैः शनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Jara\" is said to mean wasting away, and \"karu\" means dreadful. His body was \"karu\"."}},{"n":4,"text":"क्षपयामास तीव्रेण तपसेत्यत उच्यते ।\nजरत्कारुरिति ब्रह्मन्वासुकेर्भगिनी तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise one slowly wore it down with severe austerity; so he is called Jaratkaru, brahmin, and so too is Vasuki's sister."}},{"n":5,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु धर्मात्मा शौनकः प्राहसत्तदा ।\nउग्रश्रवसमामन्त्र्य उपपन्नमिति ब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the righteous Shaunaka smiled, and addressing Ugrashravas said, \"That is fitting.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"अथ कालस्य महतः स मुनिः संशितव्रतः ।\nतपस्यभिरतो धीमान्न दारानभ्यकाङ्क्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a long time the sage of strict vows, wise and absorbed in austerity, did not desire a wife."}},{"n":7,"text":"स ऊर्ध्वरेतास्तपसि प्रसक्तः\nस्वाध्यायवान्वीतभयक्लमः सन् ।\nचचार सर्वां पृथिवीं महात्मा\nन चापि दारान्मनसाप्यकाङ्क्षत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Continent, devoted to austerity and study, free of fear and weariness, the great soul wandered the whole earth and never even in thought wished for a wife."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततोऽपरस्मिन्संप्राप्ते काले कस्मिंश्चिदेव तु ।\nपरिक्षिदिति विख्यातो राजा कौरववंशभृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at a certain time there was a famed king named Parikshit, upholder of the Kuru line."}},{"n":9,"text":"यथा पाण्डुर्महाबाहुर्धनुर्धरवरो भुवि ।\nबभूव मृगयाशीलः पुरास्य प्रपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the mighty-armed Pandu, the best archer on earth, his great-grandfather had loved hunting."}},{"n":10,"text":"मृगान्विध्यन्वराहांश्च तरक्षून्महिषांस्तथा ।\nअन्यांश्च विविधान्वन्यांश्चचार पृथिवीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of the earth roamed, shooting deer, boars, hyenas, buffalo and many other forest animals."}},{"n":11,"text":"स कदाचिन्मृगं विद्ध्वा बाणेन नतपर्वणा ।\nपृष्ठतो धनुरादाय ससार गहने वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, having pierced a deer with a bent-jointed arrow, he took his bow and followed it deep into the forest."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथा हि भगवान्रुद्रो विद्ध्वा यज्ञमृगं दिवि ।\nअन्वगच्छद्धनुष्पाणिः पर्यन्वेषंस्ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the blessed Rudra, having pierced the sacrificial deer in heaven, bow in hand, searched about for it here and there,"}},{"n":13,"text":"न हि तेन मृगो विद्धो जीवन्गच्छति वै वनम् ।\nपूर्वरूपं तु तन्नूनमासीत्स्वर्गगतिं प्रति ।\nपरिक्षितस्तस्य राज्ञो विद्धो यन्नष्टवान्मृगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"so the king went; for the deer he struck never went alive into the forest. Surely it was a sign of his path to heaven that the deer Parikshit had shot disappeared."}},{"n":14,"text":"दूरं चापहृतस्तेन मृगेण स महीपतिः ।\nपरिश्रान्तः पिपासार्त आससाद मुनिं वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drawn far away by that deer, the king, weary and tormented by thirst, came upon a sage in the forest."}},{"n":15,"text":"गवां प्रचारेष्वासीनं वत्सानां मुखनिःसृतम् ।\nभूयिष्ठमुपयुञ्जानं फेनमापिबतां पयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was sitting among grazing cows and drinking the foam, mostly, that fell from the mouths of calves as they drank milk."}},{"n":16,"text":"तमभिद्रुत्य वेगेन स राजा संशितव्रतम् ।\nअपृच्छद्धनुरुद्यम्य तं मुनिं क्षुच्छ्रमान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, tired and hungry, rushed up to the sage of strict vows and, raising his bow, asked him:"}},{"n":17,"text":"भो भो ब्रह्मन्नहं राजा परिक्षिदभिमन्युजः ।\nमया विद्धो मृगो नष्टः कच्चित्त्वं दृष्टवानसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmin! I am King Parikshit, son of Abhimanyu. A deer I shot has vanished. Have you seen it?\""}},{"n":18,"text":"स मुनिस्तस्य नोवाच किंचिन्मौनव्रते स्थितः ।\nतस्य स्कन्धे मृतं सर्पं क्रुद्धो राजा समासजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage, keeping a vow of silence, said nothing to him. In anger the king hung a dead snake on his shoulder."}},{"n":19,"text":"धनुष्कोट्या समुत्क्षिप्य स चैनं समुदैक्षत ।\nन च किंचिदुवाचैनं शुभं वा यदि वाशुभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lifting it with the tip of his bow, the king looked at him, but the sage said nothing to him, good or bad."}},{"n":20,"text":"स राजा क्रोधमुत्सृज्य व्यथितस्तं तथागतम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा जगाम नगरमृषिस्त्वास्ते तथैव सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Letting go of his anger, the king felt distressed on seeing him thus, and went to his city, while the sage remained exactly as he was."}},{"n":21,"text":"तरुणस्तस्य पुत्रोऽभूत्तिग्मतेजा महातपाः ।\nशृङ्गी नाम महाक्रोधो दुष्प्रसादो महाव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage had a young son, of fierce brilliance and great austerity, named Shringin, very hot-tempered, hard to appease, strict in his vows."}},{"n":22,"text":"स देवं परमीशानं सर्वभूतहिते रतम् ।\nब्रह्माणमुपतस्थे वै काले काले सुसंयतः ।\nस तेन समनुज्ञातो ब्रह्मणा गृहमेयिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He used to attend from time to time the lord Brahma, supreme master, who is intent on the good of all beings, always self-restrained. With Brahma's leave he came home."}},{"n":23,"text":"सख्योक्तः क्रीडमानेन स तत्र हसता किल ।\nसंरम्भी कोपनोऽतीव विषकल्प ऋषेः सुतः ।\nऋषिपुत्रेण नर्मार्थं कृशेन द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"There a friend playing and laughing told him, it is said, the son of the sage, who was quick to rage and almost like poison: a thin sage's son spoke in jest, best of brahmins:"}},{"n":24,"text":"तेजस्विनस्तव पिता तथैव च तपस्विनः ।\nशवं स्कन्धेन वहति मा शृङ्गिन्गर्वितो भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your father, so brilliant and ascetic, is carrying a corpse on his shoulder. Shringin, do not be proud."}},{"n":25,"text":"व्याहरत्स्वृषिपुत्रेषु मा स्म किंचिद्वचो वदीः ।\nअस्मद्विधेषु सिद्धेषु ब्रह्मवित्सु तपस्विषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Speak no words among sages' sons. Not among such as us, perfected knowers of Brahman and ascetics."}},{"n":26,"text":"क्व ते पुरुषमानित्वं क्व ते वाचस्तथाविधाः ।\nदर्पजाः पितरं यस्त्वं द्रष्टा शवधरं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where is your manliness, where are such boastful words, born of pride, when you see your father carrying a corpse?\""}}]}]}